{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/12588-supplement-idea-eternal-servitude","id":12588,"title":"Supplement Idea: Eternal Servitude","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T01:37:58-08:00","id":12588,"title":"Supplement Idea: Eternal Servitude","content":"I'm excited for all the upcoming supplements for Mummy, of course. I'm hoping we'll even be able to get the Book of Going Westward. After that, though, if there's hopefully enough interest, I think a book of a Mummy's servants would be great and I've heard the idea tossed around here or there, too.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining three parts in it. We'd get some additional information and rules for sadikh and fasad, on par with Vampire ghouls perhaps; the core rules seem to say, in my interpretation, that a Mummy might have many sadikh although only one can be awake with it at any given time. Secondly I think some information on witnesses would be really interesting - additional background on how their supernatural senses might have come to be. In my own campaign they're often tied to the Reborn in <i>Immortals</i>, for example. They could take on a role similar to Proximi from Mage, certainly.<br /> <br /> Lastly would be the main chunk of the book, and it would deal with cults. They're the self-proclaimed &quot;Z-splat&quot; of the game and I'd love to see how they interact with each other, positively and negatively, like the guilds of the Mummies themselves.<br /> <br /> I just feel that there's plenty of material mentioned which could be expanded into this supplement, with three different types of 'servants' here. Let's not forget that the Mummies are servants in their own right, too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T06:36:54-08:00","id":12695,"title":"","content":"I can see where you are coming from with this idea. At current we have the following line-up for the Mummy setting: -<br /> <br /> 1) Core Book - Setting Book<br /> 2) Guildhalls - Fleshes out the Guilds (arguably makes them make sense in general)<br /> 3) Ready Made Characters - Gives an idea of the different types of characters that can be Mummy's (though it still has a serious Vampire feel to it)<br /> 4) Deceived - Fleshes out the last Antagonist and gives the option to play them as protagonists (also likely gives us more info on Mummy's metaphysics and history) <br /> 5) DC - Shows us how Mummy's organize themselves on a city level and how nomes function (considering the low population of Arisen in the world)<br /> 6) Sothis Ascendant - Gives us what we need for Historical games of Mummy and provides a few new Antagonists. <br /> 7) Rio - An alternate take on how Mummy's might organize themselves in a city. <br /> 8) Dreams of Avarice - Pure fluff, but like Deceived its likely to give us more of the history and metaphysics of the setting.<br /> <br /> Those 8 books encompass a lot of stuff and pretty much flesh out about 80% of the setting that was discussed in the core book I think. The two books missing (in my opinion) are =<br /> <br /> 1) A Book on Duat - This would contain more info about the realm itself, the Judges, the Nameless Gods, Ammut and her Demons e.g. Shezmu. <br /> <br /> IF book of Going Westward is made (and that I feel is a big IF) then that's what I would want it to do. <br /> <br /> 2) A Book on Servants - Details Cults and gives us more options for them, Sadikh, Fasid, mortal Sekhem Sorcerers and Witnesses should also be expanded upon in this book.<br /> <br /> Which is basically what you were suggesting Reseru. This would put Mummy on equal footing with Changeling for a &quot;limited&quot; game's number of releases (since they are both getting a &quot;Dark Era&quot; book) and I think address pretty much every aspect of the Mummy setting. <br /> <br /> CAS has mentioned that Apothesis may be the focus of a future splat which could be interesting, but I am not sure is strictly necessary. Likewise, I kinda want a book just about Shuankhsen, they are interesting characters in their own right. The inclusion of mare Bane Relics, Bane Affinities and even maybe Bane Utterances would be nice to really differentiate them from the Arisen a bit more. Plus some of their rules could afford an expansion and clearer explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T12:50:36-08:00","id":12889,"title":"","content":"Its funny you don't mention a book on Relics considering Mummy's whole purpose revolves around relics, relics are usually unique, and we have only been given a small sample of example relics. This means pretty much all storytellers have to come up with their own relics, or just use the same old small batches, or use items from other Gamelines, as Tokens and Aegis Kai Doru Relics fit the mold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:09:41-08:00","id":12946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/12588-supplement-idea-eternal-servitude?p=12889#post12889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its funny you don't mention a book on Relics considering Mummy's whole purpose revolves around relics, relics are usually unique, and we have only been given a small sample of example relics. This means pretty much all storytellers have to come up with their own relics, or just use the same old small batches, or use items from other Gamelines, as Tokens and Aegis Kai Doru Relics fit the mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't list a book of Relics for a few reasons -<br /> <br /> 1) We've already been told that we'll get more in upcoming books (Sothis Ascendant) and if the splat books that have come out already are any sign Deceived, DC and Rio might also have some more.<br /> 2) Its easy to re-purpose items already published. In my Mummy game I used Reliquaries, Hunter (and its splat books) and Changeling (and its splat books). Its would be pretty easy to adapt the Giest Memento's as well. <br /> 3) I don't think we need a whole book dedicated to just giving us item options, that's kinda dull and honestly I can't see it filling more then 50 pages at best. At best it's an on-line PDF extra like Goblin Markets was for Changeling. <br /> <br /> Obviously, this is just my point of view. If there is enough demand for a book just for relics I am sure they might make one. Which I'll likely buy. I want to support Mummy so we get the Book of Going Westword. <br /> <br /> Honestly at the moment I have no idea how well the Mummy line is doing. The Core was the 4th most successful Kickstarter and Guildhalls hit number 1 on DriveThruRPG for about a week, but I have no idea if that really means anything. The last time I heard White Wolf talk about profit was when Changeling came out and made a huge amount of money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:45:55-08:00","id":13266,"title":"","content":"There's a lot I'm expecting for the line that I think is going to get a home already. I'm the kind of guy that thinks all the books' talk of mortal sorcerers means they'll get their own Mummy-specific rules somewhere already on schedule, as well as new antagonists like the nowhere-near-as-successful-attempts at supernatural mummies of other cultures which I assume would be put in Sothis Ascends - which is probably where a lot of relics will go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T02:01:29-08:00","id":13876,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well it's seemed to me that they've shilled the decieved as masters of mummy magic, so perhaps the rules for sorcerers will be included in that book, or sothis ascendant since I would imagine the sorcerers have been encountered by mummies throughout the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}